# Keep the Docker build context clean. The Dockerfile does `COPY profiles/ profiles/`,
# which would otherwise ship generated state, course notes and research into the image.
# For a release, build from the clean export (export/build_export.py); this is the belt.

# --- WIP / research / campaign areas (never in the product image) ---
results/
evals-to-review/
reviews/
bounded-oracles/
internal/
notes/
decks/
labs/
labs-ctf/
export/
*.md.bak

# --- generated state that accumulates inside profiles/ ---
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.log
**/mock-audit*.jsonl
**/*.local-*
**/*.bak
**/*.sqlite
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite-journal

# --- course / research files that live inside shipped profile dirs ---
**/MODULE*.md
**/*-RECORD.md
**/CTF-SUMMARY.md
**/FINDINGS.md
**/HIGHLIGHTS.md
profiles/*/classroom.py
profiles/*/llm08-exercise/
profiles/*/notes/
profiles/*/proposal*.md

# --- profiles that are not supported targets in the first release ---
profiles/investigations/

# --- secrets / local / vcs / scratch ---
.env
.env.*
.git/
.venv/
venv/
*.pem
INSTALL-KALI.md
